{"task_id": "HumanEval/32", "solution": "import math\n\n\ndef poly(xs: list, x: float):\n    \"\"\"\n    Evaluates polynomial with coefficients xs at point x.\n    return xs[0] + xs[1] * x + xs[1] * x^2 + .... xs[n] * x^n\n    \"\"\"\n    return sum([coeff * math.pow(x, i) for i, coeff in enumerate(xs)])\n\n\ndef find_zero(xs: list):\n    \"\"\" xs are coefficients of a polynomial.\n    find_zero find x such that poly(x) = 0.\n    find_zero returns only only zero point, even if there are many.\n    Moreover, find_zero only takes list xs having even number of coefficients\n    and largest non zero coefficient as it guarantees\n    a solution.\n    >>> round(find_zero([1, 2]), 2) # f(x) = 1 + 2x\n    -0.5\n    >>> round(find_zero([-6, 11, -6, 1]), 2) # (x - 1) * (x - 2) * (x - 3) = -6 + 11x - 6x^2 + x^3\n    1.0\n    \"\"\"\n    # Bisection method parameters, hardcoded as per design context and prompt constraints.\n    low, high = -100.0, 100.0\n    tolerance = 1e-6\n    max_iterations = 1000\n\n    # Assume inputs are valid and a solution is guaranteed as per the docstring.\n    # No explicit input validation or error raising for edge cases due to prompt constraints.\n\n    f_low = poly(xs, low)\n    f_high = poly(xs, high)\n\n    # For odd-degree polynomials with real coefficients, a real root is guaranteed.\n    # The search range is assumed to be wide enough to bracket a root initially.\n\n    for _ in range(max_iterations):\n        mid = (low + high) / 2\n        f_mid = poly(xs, mid)\n\n        if abs(f_mid) < tolerance:\n            return mid\n\n        # Determine which half of the interval the root lies in based on sign change.\n        if f_low * f_mid < 0:\n            high = mid\n            f_high = f_mid\n        else:\n            low = mid\n            f_low = f_mid\n\n    # If the loop completes without returning, a root was not found within tolerance and iterations.\n    # As per prompt constraints, no exception should be raised. Return the midpoint of the final interval.\n    return (low + high) / 2"}
