{"task_id": "HumanEval/47", "solution": "def median(l: list):\n    \"\"\"Return median of elements in the list l.\n    >>> median([3, 1, 2, 4, 5])\n    3\n    >>> median([-10, 4, 6, 1000, 10, 20])\n    15.0\n    \"\"\"\n    sorted_l = sorted(l)\n    n = len(sorted_l)\n\n    if n % 2 == 1:\n        # For an odd number of elements, the median is the middle element.\n        median_val = sorted_l[n // 2]\n    else:\n        # For an even number of elements, the median is the average of the two middle elements.\n        mid1 = sorted_l[n // 2 - 1]\n        mid2 = sorted_l[n // 2]\n        median_val = (mid1 + mid2) / 2.0\n\n    # Return as int if the median is a whole number, otherwise float.\n    if median_val == int(median_val):\n        return int(median_val)\n    return float(median_val)"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/46", "solution": "def fib4(n: int):\n    \"\"\"Computes the n-th element of the Fib4 number sequence iteratively.\n    The sequence is defined by fib4(n) = fib4(n-1) + fib4(n-2) + fib4(n-3) + fib4(n-4) for n > 3.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    elif n == 1:\n        return 0\n    elif n == 2:\n        return 2\n    elif n == 3:\n        return 0\n\n    # Initialize with the first four values: fib4(0), fib4(1), fib4(2), fib4(3).\n    fib_values = [0, 0, 2, 0] \n\n    for i in range(4, n + 1):\n        next_fib = fib_values[i-1] + fib_values[i-2] + fib_values[i-3] + fib_values[i-4]\n        fib_values.append(next_fib)\n    \n    return fib_values[n]"}
