{"task_id": "HumanEval/64", "solution": "def vowels_count(s):\n    \"\"\"Write a function vowels_count which takes a string representing\n    a word as input and returns the number of vowels in the string.\n    Vowels in this case are 'a', 'e', 'i', 'o', 'u'. Here, 'y' is also a\n    vowel, but only when it is at the end of the given word.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not s:\n        return 0\n\n    VOWELS_SET = {'a', 'e', 'i', 'o', 'u'}\n    count = 0\n    s_lower = s.lower()\n\n    for char in s_lower:\n        if char in VOWELS_SET:\n            count += 1\n\n    if s_lower.endswith('y'):\n        count += 1\n\n    return count"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/63", "solution": "_fibfib_memo = {}\n\n\ndef fibfib(n: int):\n    \"\"\"Computes the n-th FibFib number using memoization.\"\"\"\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a non-negative integer.\")\n\n    if n in _fibfib_memo:\n        return _fibfib_memo[n]\n\n    if n == 0 or n == 1:\n        result = 0\n    elif n == 2:\n        result = 1\n    else:\n        result = fibfib(n - 1) + fibfib(n - 2) + fibfib(n - 3)\n\n    _fibfib_memo[n] = result\n    return result"}
